/T (These findings also point to a broader gap in the financial infrastructure that supports government-funded work. While nonprofit organizations and Tribes are expected to implement publicly funded programs, many lack access to the working capital required to manage reimbursement cycles. As a result, organizations must rely on reserves, borrowing, or other stopgap measures to bridge funding gaps.)
